## Overview
#c1[overview,i5] Order totals are computed by summing line subtotals and weights, applying a single discount code, then adding a shipping fee based on weight and subtotal.
  > src/orders.ts::orderTotal #dd631e05bf9f
  > src/orders.ts:1 #7c33608098bc
  > src/pricing.ts:15-19 #5e38de870e63
  > src/pricing.ts::applyCode #8771bf83e15f
  > src/pricing.ts:3-7 #d21948eae853
  > src/pricing.ts::shippingFee #52d3f81cc48d
#c2[overview,i5] Shipping fees charge a base of $5.00 plus $1.20 per started kilogram, are free for orders ≥ $50.00, and reject parcels over 30 kg.
  > src/pricing.ts:3-7 #d21948eae853
  > src/pricing.ts::shippingFee #52d3f81cc48d
  > docs/policy.md::Shipping #70540f02d196
#c3[overview,i5] Only one discount code may be used per order; `WELCOME10` gives 10% off, `SPRING5` gives $5 off, and discounts never reduce the total below zero.
  > docs/policy.md::"Discount codes" #e1577f95056e
  > src/pricing.ts:15-19 #5e38de870e63
  > src/pricing.ts::applyCode #8771bf83e15f
#c4[overview,i5] Order status transitions follow a forward‑only map, allowing refunds only after payment and recording delivery timestamps on transition to "delivered".
  > src/orders.ts::NEXT #01102ea406bc
  > src/orders.ts::transition #15c6693b8866
#c5[overview,i5] Customers can request full refunds within 14 days of delivery or any time before shipping; nightly workers process approved refunds with no restocking fee.
  > docs/policy.md::Refunds #10997ef53cdd
  > worker/refunds.py:5 #5e51e9c176ba
  > worker/refunds.py:6 #1d736265949d
  > worker/refunds.py::refundable #f666469b81c4
  > worker/refunds.py::refund_amount #bcbb8752bf45
  > worker/refunds.py:1 #dfa367b0c20e
#c6[overview,i5] All monetary values are stored as integer cents to avoid floating‑point rounding errors.
  > src/pricing.ts:1 #e9fc87c7c197
  > src/pricing.ts:3-7 #d21948eae853
#c7[overview,i5] The Order model includes line items (sku, unit price, quantity, weight), an optional discount code, status, and optional delivery timestamp.
  > src/orders.ts::Line #57f6ce006f11
  > src/orders.ts::Order #66d92fa57ed2
#c8[overview,i5] The refund worker skips unapproved or out‑of‑window requests, logs actions, and returns the IDs of orders successfully refunded.
  > worker/refunds.py::run #b3d349a19ab4
  > worker/refunds.py::RefundError #c70edc5b0830

## docs
#c9[i5] Shipping costs a base fee of 5.00 plus 1.20 per started kilogram.
  > docs/policy.md::Shipping #70540f02d196
#c10[i5] Orders with a total of 50.00 or more qualify for free shipping.
  > docs/policy.md::Shipping #70540f02d196
#c11[i4] The carrier refuses parcels over 30 kg, so such orders cannot be placed.
  > docs/policy.md::Shipping #70540f02d196
#c12[i5] Customers may request a refund up to 14 days after delivery or any time before the order ships.
  > docs/policy.md::Refunds #10997ef53cdd
#c13[i4] Refunds are for the full amount, approved by a support agent, and paid by the refund worker each night.
  > docs/policy.md::Refunds #10997ef53cdd
#c14[i3] Only one discount code can be applied per order.
  > docs/policy.md::"Discount codes" #e1577f95056e
#c15[i3] `WELCOME10` provides a 10% discount on items, while `SPRING5` provides a 5.00 monetary discount.
  > docs/policy.md::"Discount codes" #e1577f95056e
#c16[i3] A discount never reduces item cost below zero, and shipping is calculated on the price before the discount.
  > docs/policy.md::"Discount codes" #e1577f95056e

## src
#c17[i4] The module imports the functions applyCode and shippingFee from the "./pricing" module.
  > src/orders.ts:1 #7c33608098bc
#c18[i5] The Line interface defines a sku string, unitPrice number, quantity number, and weightKg number.
  > src/orders.ts::Line #57f6ce006f11
#c19[i5] The Order interface includes an id string, an array of Line objects, an optional code string, a status limited to specific literals, and an optional deliveredAt string.
  > src/orders.ts::Order #66d92fa57ed2
#c20[i5] orderTotal calculates subtotal as the sum of unitPrice × quantity, weight as the sum of weightKg × quantity, then returns applyCode(subtotal, order.code) plus shippingFee(weight, subtotal).
  > src/orders.ts::orderTotal #dd631e05bf9f
#c21[i4] The NEXT constant maps each Order status to an array of allowed next statuses, enforcing forward-only progression and refunds only after payment.
  > src/orders.ts::NEXT #01102ea406bc
#c22[i5] transition throws an Error if the desired status is not listed in NEXT for the current status; otherwise it returns a new Order with the updated status and sets deliveredAt to the current ISO timestamp when transitioning to "delivered".
  > src/orders.ts::transition #15c6693b8866
#c23[i5] Prices are stored as integer cents to avoid floating‑point rounding.
  > src/pricing.ts:1 #e9fc87c7c197
#c24[i5] BASE_FEE is 500 cents, PER_KG is 120 cents, MAX_WEIGHT_KG is 30 kg, and FREE_SHIPPING_FROM is 5000 cents.
  > src/pricing.ts:3-7 #d21948eae853
#c25[i5] shippingFee throws an Error when weightKg exceeds MAX_WEIGHT_KG.
  > src/pricing.ts::shippingFee #52d3f81cc48d
#c26[i4] If subtotal is at least FREE_SHIPPING_FROM, shippingFee returns 0 (free shipping).
  > src/pricing.ts::shippingFee #52d3f81cc48d
#c27[i4] Otherwise shippingFee returns BASE_FEE plus PER_KG multiplied by the ceiling of weightKg.
  > src/pricing.ts::shippingFee #52d3f81cc48d
#c28[i5] CODES maps discount identifiers to either a percent or a fixed amount, and each code applies only once per order and never reduces the total below zero.
  > src/pricing.ts:15-19 #5e38de870e63
#c29[i3] applyCode returns the original subtotal when no code is provided.
  > src/pricing.ts::applyCode #8771bf83e15f
#c30[i4] applyCode throws an Error for unknown discount codes after converting the input to uppercase.
  > src/pricing.ts::applyCode #8771bf83e15f
#c31[i4] When a code has a percent field, applyCode calculates the discount as the subtotal multiplied by that percent, rounded to the nearest cent.
  > src/pricing.ts::applyCode #8771bf83e15f
#c32[i4] applyCode ensures the final total is never negative by taking the maximum of 0 and subtotal minus the discount.
  > src/pricing.ts::applyCode #8771bf83e15f

## worker
#c33[i5] The module defines a nightly Refund worker that processes approved refund requests.
  > worker/refunds.py:1 #dfa367b0c20e
#c34[i5] REFUND_WINDOW_DAYS is set to 14, limiting refunds to within 14 days of delivery.
  > worker/refunds.py:5 #5e51e9c176ba
#c35[i4] RESTOCKING_FEE_PERCENT is 0, meaning no restocking fee is applied to refunds.
  > worker/refunds.py:6 #1d736265949d
#c36[i5] Refundable returns True for orders with status "paid" regardless of delivery date.
  > worker/refunds.py::refundable #f666469b81c4
#c37[i5] For delivered orders, refundable checks that the current time minus deliveredAt is ≤ REFUND_WINDOW_DAYS.
  > worker/refunds.py::refundable #f666469b81c4
#c38[i4] refund_amount computes the refund as order_total minus the restocking fee percentage (integer division).
  > worker/refunds.py::refund_amount #bcbb8752bf45
#c39[i5] run iterates over requests, skips unapproved ones, logs and skips those outside the refund window, and calls gateway.refund for valid requests.
  > worker/refunds.py::run #b3d349a19ab4
#c40[i4] run returns a list of order IDs that were successfully refunded.
  > worker/refunds.py::run #b3d349a19ab4
#c41[i2] RefundError is defined as a custom exception type for refund-related errors.
  > worker/refunds.py::RefundError #c70edc5b0830

